cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "TensorPyPy: Tensor-Aware Meta-Tracing JIT Compiler"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Izawa
    given-names: Yusuke
    affiliation: Tokyo Metropolitan University
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  TensorPyPy is a fork of PyPy whose RPython meta-tracing JIT carries a
  tensor runtime, MetaTensor. Traced chains of tensor operations become fused
  GPU kernels. The code is in rpython/metatensor/, pypy/module/_metatensor/
  and lib_pypy/tensorpypy/, and benchmark/ holds the MetaTensor benchmarks.
  Note: TensorPyPy is one part of the larger MOTION study. benchmark/motion/
  (the MOTION leave transition, its rule audit and a hand-written adapter)
  belongs to that wider study and is not described by this record.
keywords:
  - PyPy
  - RPython
  - meta-tracing JIT
  - tensor compiler
  - kernel fusion
  - GPU
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "MetaTensor: Tensor Fusion in a Meta-Tracing Compiler"
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23298877
    authors:
      - family-names: Izawa
        given-names: Yusuke
